12292	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-cfd2cee8e5504584b372584ce8e623df","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:22:15.179Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed exclusions preserve upstream ac1 and the promise to expose every automatable gh operation.","evidence":"DEF §6.5 ac1 requires an operation gh supports to be reachable through a named family tool. The installed gh help explicitly documents noninteractive logout: 'gh auth logout --hostname enterprise.internal --user monalisa'. Codespace cp also accepts an explicit '--codespace' selector. The LLD excludes these as requiring a person, and separately excludes automatable configuration operations without an approved upstream scope amendment. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Correct the interactive classification and include these operations, or obtain an explicit upstream amendment identifying accepted exclusions before claiming ac1 is met.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The family contracts specify enough operation coverage and schemas to implement the complete registry.","evidence":"LLD §§2.5–2.6 specify only 'op: enum of the group's automatable subcommands' and '...per-op fields'; §10 defers the exact list to the plan. Unlike the existing concrete registrations in registerGhTools, there is no enumerated operation-to-tool mapping, per-operation required fields, output variants, or complete approval mapping to assess. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/index.ts]","action":"Supply the operation inventory and per-operation contracts now, including command → tool/op ownership and compatibility with existing tools. A table is sufficient; an ERD or UX mock is unnecessary for this registry change. No generated visual is claimed or available to verify.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Current gh overrides are limited to 60, 120 and 180 seconds, and legacy requiresApproval flags still need replacing.","evidence":"ghRepoCloneTool calls ghExec with 'timeoutMs: 600_000'; ghPrCreateTool uses 'timeoutMs: 90_000'. Existing mutation definitions already declare 'approval: common', and the approval-mapping test asserts that no builtin declares requiresApproval. The migration baseline omits these timeout values and describes an already-completed approval-field migration. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Update the baseline and compatibility discussion to include clone's 600→120 second and PR creation's 90→120 second changes, and describe approval-class refinement rather than legacy-field replacement.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc3 already provides serial text conversion, schema checking, cross-checking and one escalation tier.","evidence":"convertText accepts ConversionRequest containing rawText, schema and keyValues plus ToolDeps. Its module-level takeSlot queue serializes conversions, and its tier loop uses tools.convert followed by tools.convert.escalate. ATTEMPTS_PER_TIER is 2; failed conversion returns ok:false. [files: src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Reuse this implementation and explicitly adapt its ConversionFailure to ToolFailure conversion-failed while preserving the raw text.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The timeout change-site inventory covers every override that must be removed.","evidence":"§3.4 lists helpers.ts, actions.ts, release.ts and repo.ts. However, ghPrDiffTool uses 60_000, ghPrCreateTool 90_000, ghPrMergeTool 180_000, and ghIssueCreateTool 60_000. Changing the default and only the listed sites leaves commands outside the promised uniform 120-second limit. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/issue.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Add pr.ts and issue.ts to the timeout inventory and assert that every gh invocation uses the centralized deadline without an override.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The declared Tool-returning wrapper preserves the typed definition required by callTool.","evidence":"The proposed signature is 'withGhFailureNet(tool: Tool): Tool'. Actual callTool requires TypedTool, whose inputSchema and outputSchema are required TSchema values. Tool instead declares inputSchema as Record<string, unknown> and outputSchema as optional, so this wrapper erases the required schema types even if its input was inferred correctly. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Make the wrapper preserve the concrete typed definition and require outputSchema in its input constraint. Export converted definitions with inferred schemas rather than widening them to Tool; add a compile-time callTool usage check.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Standardizing legacy list results to {items} is an additive change that preserves the existing output contract.","evidence":"ghRepoListTool currently returns data:{count: repos.length, repos}; ghRunListTool returns data:{count: runs.length, runs}; ghWorkflowListTool returns data:{count: workflows.length, workflows}. §3.1 specifies that 'a list read returns { items }', while HLD §7 says an existing tool's input and output stay as they are unless the schema only names what it already returned. Existing structured data is not a newly added payload. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"Schema the existing data shapes in place. If items is useful, add it while retaining existing fields and test those fields explicitly. Document any intentional exception through the upstream compatibility process.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Deferring external workflow caller migration to s7 respects the HLD ownership boundary.","evidence":"HLD §7 assigns the cutover of direct spawn call sites to s7 after the tool families are complete. The LLD explicitly leaves gates.ts, tracker-auto.ts, bugfix/tracker.ts and github.ts wrappers to s7, while consuming sc2–sc5 rather than replacing their public contracts. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Retain that separation. Keep any shared-classifier extraction behavior-preserving for existing git exports and callers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A Tool-level failure wrapper can classify all subprocess failures from the existing execute results.","evidence":"shellFail converts ShellResult to output/format/success/error and discards timedOut, spawnError and stdoutTruncated. More seriously, ghRunViewTool computes 'logBody = logs.code === 0 ? logs.stdout : logs.stderr' and ultimately returns success:true even when the log subprocess failed. A wrapper around execute cannot reliably recover those flags or detect this swallowed failure. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Specify classification and propagation at the ghExec/helper boundary, with per-invocation outcomes available to each tool. Explicitly handle secondary-command failures and truncation before parsing or rendering, including gh_run_view's log call.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The designed ghExec and schema-secret annotation support stdin delivery and approval redaction for value fields.","evidence":"ghExec delegates to runShell, which spawns with 'stdio: [ignore, pipe, pipe]' and accepts no stdin option; the proposed ghExec signature also has no stdin. runShellBytes already supports stdin. Approval-policy display masks keys matching SECRET_KEY, which does not match 'value'; buildApprovalRequest never reads inputSchema and invokes custom previews with the original input. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Design a gh stdin execution path using the existing byte helper or an explicit helper extension. Define tool-local masking for both approval arguments and previews, or coordinate a schema-aware shared-contract change with its owner. Test a literal value key and confirm the value appears in neither argv nor approval content.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream s5 acceptance criterion has an identified proving test category.","evidence":"DEF §6.5 defines ac1–ac6. LLD §6 maps them respectively to coverage/registry tests, output-schema and conversion tests, approval tests, missing-tool/sign-in tests, deadline tests, and legacy compatibility tests. These are proposed tests, not evidence that implementation already passes. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Retain all six mappings and make the coverage tests verify executable tool/op cases rather than registration alone.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Updating the approval snapshot alone makes the existing s3 audit compatible with the proposed gh classes.","evidence":"approval-class-mapping.test.ts fixes snapshot.length at 228, expects former true flags to have the literal approval value 'common' except three named git tools, and expects former reads to declare approval:undefined. The LLD proposes a function on each gh tool and destructive classes for several former common tools. Its snapshot update does not specify changes to these assertions. [files: src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/fixtures/approval-snapshot.json, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Include the audit test itself in the change sites. Preserve the historical snapshot and add explicit s5 expectations for refined classes and new tools, following the separate addedByS4 precedent instead of rewriting historical evidence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":6,"med":3,"low":3,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T10:22:15.179Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
433	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"bb20bf8948cd4cf78b1a288585a81046","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:24:28.269Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":1,"contentHash":"ceb926b770bfcb9332b7d5a0aa2e34e4b7d6a3f1bdcb17da49590eed234a4342"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":6,"med":3,"low":3}}}}}
10495	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-5f335c7993a3ce68d0c3ea9356a94add","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:31:31.172Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The operation inventory consistently makes closing operations destructive.","evidence":"The LLD promises 'closing, merging and deleting are destructive', but §3.2 assigns gh_project_manage close to common. approval-policy.ts explicitly says common calls run without asking in auto mode; destructive calls always ask. Building this row would permit closing a project without the promised approval. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Classify project close as destructive and update the inventory and approval tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The gh exclusions were accepted by the user and recorded in docs/plans/tool-registry.md.","evidence":"I searched the decision document and read its relevant coverage decisions. It records accepted git exclusions under 's4 split', but I found no acceptance record for the LLD's gh exclusions, including config set and extension operations. DEF s5 ac1 still requires every supported gh operation. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Link the actual gh exclusion approval or obtain and record that decision before treating these exclusions as authorized.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current helper defaults to 30 seconds, loses process flags in tool failures, and run view can report a failed log read as success.","evidence":"helpers.ts uses 'timeoutMs: opts.timeoutMs ?? 30_000'; shellFail returns output/format/success/error without failure metadata. The complete ghRunViewTool implementation uses 'logs.code === 0 ? logs.stdout : logs.stderr' and subsequently returns 'success: true'. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Retain these verified behaviors as the baseline for the planned corrections.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing typed-call, conversion, secret masking and stdin capabilities support the proposed reuse.","evidence":"call-tool.ts defines TypedTool using input/output TSchema and derives callTool input/result through Static. convert-text.ts accepts schema, rawText and required keyValues with ToolDeps and serializes conversions. approval-policy.ts's SECRET_KEY regex includes 'secret', so secretValue is masked in the generic preview. runShellBytes accepts 'stdin?: Uint8Array | string'. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Reuse these implementations; preserve their concrete types and explicitly adapt the byte result as noted under error paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"ghFailureOf's synchronous signature can perform the stated ambiguous-authentication probe.","evidence":"The LLD declares 'ghFailureOf(...): ToolFailure' but requires it to run 'gh auth status once' when authentication text is ambiguous. The existing execution primitives runShell and runShellBytes return Promises. The declared synchronous boundary cannot await that subprocess result. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Make classification asynchronous and update callers, or perform the bounded auth probe in ghExec and include its result in GhOutcome.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The family-tool contracts sufficiently specify typed inputs and outputs for all new operations.","evidence":"§2.7 supplies only '{ op: enum; ...per-op fields }' and generic list/view/mutation descriptions, while §10 defers exact fields to the plan. Installed gh 2.46.0 help shows auth status, status and codespace logs have no --json option. These reads cannot use the stated generic 'object gh --json gives' contract, and no parsing/conversion shape is specified for them. Existing Tool and callTool require actual schemas. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Specify per-op required/optional inputs, output fields, command construction and text parsing/conversion paths before approval. Document tool-to-op ownership and mapping in a table; a separate ERD is unnecessary for this registry-only change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The compatibility description lists all intended changes to existing success/error behavior.","evidence":"§7 lists only timeout increases and failed run-log reads as visible changes. However, ghPrDiffTool currently returns 'success: true' with a truncated diff and data.truncated, and ghRunViewTool similarly returns capped logs successfully. The proposed failure net rejects every stdoutTruncated result. The current caps are 256 KiB for diff and 128 KiB for logs by default, so this is not confined to the documented 4 MiB case. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Explicitly record truncated-read rejection as a compatibility change and add fixtures at the existing configurable/default caps. Preserve existing successful data fields when adding converted content.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed per-job timeout policy conforms to the effective upstream performance contract.","evidence":"HLD §6 states 'gh commands time out after 120 seconds'; §5.5 assigns s5 'the 120 second time limit'. The LLD instead specifies 30–600 seconds and acknowledges that its nonFunctional.retarget amendment 'has to be filed and approved'. The supplied design therefore knowingly departs from its current upstream contract. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"File and obtain approval for the performance amendment, then reference the effective amended contract in this LLD.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"GhOutcome preserves all failures relevant to delivering secret stdin through runShellBytes.","evidence":"GhOutcome declares result: ShellResult, but runShellBytes returns ShellBytesResult with Uint8Array stdout and additional 'stdinError', 'stderrOverflow' and 'aborted' fields. Its body records stdin write errors without necessarily changing the child exit code. The LLD's classification precondition names only spawnError, timedOut, truncated or nonzero exit, so a code-zero stdin delivery failure can escape classification. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Define the byte-to-text adapter and preserve/classify stdinError, stderrOverflow and aborted before accepting success. Add a fixture where gh exits successfully without consuming the supplied secret.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Executor output-schema rejection preserves the raw gh output in failure.original.","evidence":"The LLD says an executor schema failure retains 'the raw output in failure.original'. executor.ts instead passes 'result.output' to failed(), which truncates it to 4000 characters. Existing gh tools render markdown into result.output, so this is neither necessarily raw stdout nor the complete original. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Validate parsed gh data inside the family boundary and attach the intended raw diagnostic there, or specify the existing rendered, truncated executor diagnostic accurately without redesigning sc2.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream s5 acceptance criterion has an explicit planned proving test.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.5 ac1–ac6 with LLD §6: coverage/registration and fake-gh operation tests map to ac1; schema/conversion/type tests to ac2; approval tests to ac3; missing-tool/sign-in tests to ac4; timeout tests to ac5; legacy-id/input/result fixtures to ac6. These are proposed tests, not executed implementation evidence. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Keep the six mappings and extend their cases for the confirmed contract and error-path corrections above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":4,"low":4,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T10:31:31.172Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
