9121	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-24dcbb2244fb8bb2e7c862fb7a079bff","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:49:33.217Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The operation contracts expose exactly the supported flags, apart from accepted exclusions.","evidence":"Installed gh 2.46.0 help documents issue develop '--list' and secret set '--env-file'; neither appears in GhOpContracts or the accepted exclusions. A command-level coverage row would still pass while these capabilities remain unreachable. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Complete the per-operation flag inventory, explicitly resolve omissions, and test flag coverage as well as command coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The exclusions and replacement of the fixed gh timeout reflect upstream user decisions.","evidence":"The 's5 decisions' section explicitly accepts the listed exclusions, includes logout/switch/cp/logs/ports, and says the HLD performance line 'is to be read as this table'. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain these decisions and complete the acknowledged amendment bookkeeping.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current gh execution defaults to 30 seconds, with the stated ten explicit timeout overrides.","evidence":"helpers.ts uses 'timeoutMs: opts.timeoutMs ?? 30_000'. Reading the ghExec call inventory confirms the ten overrides across issue, pr, actions, repo and release match the design's values. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/issue.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/release.ts]","action":"Preserve these lower bounds in the table.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"gh_run_view currently returns success with stderr as logs when its log command fails.","evidence":"Its execute body assigns 'const logBody = logs.code === 0 ? logs.stdout : logs.stderr' and subsequently returns 'success: true' with data containing runId and jobs. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Keep the explicitly documented correction to this behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShellBytes and the typed call helper already provide the shared capabilities this Story proposes to consume.","evidence":"runShellBytes accepts stdin and exposes stderrOverflow, aborted and stdinError. callTool<T extends TypedTool> derives input and result types through Static<T['inputSchema']> and Static<T['outputSchema']>. The analyzer returned incomplete grounding, so these contracts were checked directly in their complete implementations. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Keep the gh adapter local and preserve the concrete schema types.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"GhOpContracts consistently applies destructive approval to forced overwrites of remote objects.","evidence":"The design promises destructive approval for forced remote overwrites, but lists release upload with clobber and label create/clone with force as common. Installed help says upload --clobber 'Overwrite existing assets of the same name', label clone --force 'Overwrite labels', and label create --force updates an existing label. approval-policy.ts allows common calls without asking in auto mode. [files: src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Add input-dependent destructive rows for these overwrite cases and cover them in approval tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Changing all captures to runShellBytes preserves the existing capped output text exactly.","evidence":"runShell appends a decoded stdout chunk only when accumulated bytes remain within maxBytes; it drops the entire crossing chunk. runShellBytes instead retains the available prefix using 'chunk.subarray(0, room)'. Thus the same oversized diff/log stream can produce different text and diffBytes after the adapter change, contrary to the exact legacy-answer invariant. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Explicitly accept and document this capture correction or design a compatibility adapter; add fixtures whose chunks cross the cap, including UTF-8 boundaries.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The planned approval snapshot changes address the existing test's enforcement without rewriting historical rows.","evidence":"approval-class-mapping.test.ts asserts fixed 'common' outside PER_INPUT_SINCE_S4, compares serialized input schemas with historical rows, and reads addedByS4 separately. The proposed S5 sets and separate added list directly address those enforcement points. [files: src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Retain separate schema identity and behavioral compatibility tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design consumes the existing executor contracts without redesigning other Stories' implementation boundaries.","evidence":"executor.ts already validates typed inputs before approval, denies unapproved destructive calls, validates output data and truncates failure.original to 4000 characters. convert-text.ts already provides schema validation, required keyValues and one escalation tier. The gh adapter can use these unchanged. There is no persistent entity relationship or UX change requiring an ERD or UX mock; the signatures and interaction table adequately describe these dependencies. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Keep changes within gh definitions, helpers and their registry/tests; leave shared executor and conversion policy ownership intact.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"An exit-zero process that does not read its secret input is reliably detected through stdinError.","evidence":"runShellBytes only sets stdinError in 'child.stdin.on(\"error\", ...)' and sends input with 'child.stdin.end(options.stdin)'. A successful pipe write can buffer a small secret even if the child never reads it; no error or consumption acknowledgement is guaranteed. The design's exit-zero/non-reading detection claim therefore exceeds this unchanged helper's capability. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Limit the guarantee to reported stdin write errors and gh's exit status, or define an additional verifiable acknowledgement. Do not equate a successful write with confirmed consumption.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed coverage tests establish the claimed operation-and-flag completeness.","evidence":"The strategy checks help command lists against GH_COVERAGE and checks each declared op's argv against fixtures. Neither checks supported flags missing from the declared contracts. The installed help omissions identified for issue develop and secret set can survive both tests. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/index.ts]","action":"Add an independently reviewed supported-flag inventory with explicit exclusions and tests comparing it against schemas/argv builders; retain command coverage and fake-process tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":4,"med":1,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T10:49:33.217Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
