10595	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-e37460f6313656b40a88d65207357a2c","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:58:12.041Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed operation surface preserves the upstream prohibition on raw passthrough.","evidence":"DEF §3 excludes raw passthrough. GhOpContracts nevertheless exposes codespace cp's expand flag. Installed gh 2.46.0 help says this treats remote arguments as 'a Bash expression' and supports 'environment variables, and backticks'. This permits arbitrary remote command execution through a nominal copy operation. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Exclude expand explicitly in GH_FLAGS and reject it in the schema, or obtain an explicit upstream scope decision before exposing shell evaluation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every rename operation is classified destructive.","evidence":"§2.5 requires destructive for 'rename', but GhOpContracts specifies 'gh_gist ... rename [common 60]'. Installed gh help confirms this operation renames a gist file. approval-policy.ts allows common operations to run without asking in auto mode. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Classify gist rename destructive and add an explicit test for its resolved approval class.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The legacy gh helper defaults to 30 seconds, and the proposed existing-tool limits do not shorten its explicit overrides.","evidence":"helpers.ts uses 'timeoutMs: opts.timeoutMs ?? 30_000'. The ten explicit overrides in issue, pr, repo, release and actions match the listed 60–600 second limits, including PR create 90 and merge 180. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/issue.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/release.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Preserve these values in the table and regression fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"gh_run_view currently succeeds when its log subprocess fails and returns only runId and jobs as data.","evidence":"The complete execute body selects 'logs.code === 0 ? logs.stdout : logs.stderr', then returns 'success: true, data: { runId: id, jobs: payload.jobs ?? [] }'. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Retain explicit compatibility documentation for the proposed failure behavior and additive truncated field.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShellBytes supplies the stdin and outcome information required by the proposed gh adapter without changing shell-helper.ts.","evidence":"ShellBytesOptions accepts stdin and signal; ShellBytesResult includes stdout bytes, stderrOverflow, aborted and stdinError. Its implementation retains the stdout prefix up to stdoutLimit, kills the process group on timeout and records stdin errors. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Use the existing stdin option and preserve all outcome fields in the adapter.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing shared typed-call and conversion facilities have the shapes the design intends to consume.","evidence":"callTool derives input and data types from Static<T['inputSchema']> and Static<T['outputSchema']>. convertText accepts a schema, rawText, keyValues and deps; it serializes calls and escalates once after cheap-tier attempts. The analyzer returned an off-target, incomplete map, so these conclusions use direct implementation reads. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts]","action":"Keep concrete schema types through the wrapper and supply conversion deps and keyValues explicitly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"GhOpContracts completely specifies the new operations' typed inputs and outputs.","evidence":"The proposed source-of-truth table leaves search inputs as 'the group's own filter flags', codespace view output as 'the view fields', and GPG list as 'tab parser' without columns or types. §2.8 requires output discriminated by op, but the listed generic output shapes omit the discriminator. These details are deferred to the plan despite being the contracts this LLD is meant to fix. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Supply explicit per-op fields, requiredness, exclusive combinations, output properties and discriminator placement before implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing result envelopes and schema snapshots can be preserved without a stored-data migration.","evidence":"The inspected gh implementations return transient ToolResult.data objects, including {count, repos}, {count, runs}, {count, workflows}, diff metadata and run metadata. approval-class-mapping.test.ts compares serialized input schemas against the 228-tool snapshot and separately reads addedByS4. The proposed separate S5 additions and explicit exceptions fit this existing mechanism. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Keep the 228 historical rows unchanged and test any declared schema exception against accepted old inputs.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design consumes shared approval and execution contracts without redesigning their ownership.","evidence":"Tool.approval already accepts a fixed class or input function. executeTool validates inputs, asks the daemon-owned gate, runs the tool, validates success data and then runs hooks. The proposed family mapping and adapter remain within gh ownership. The interaction table adequately identifies these dependency directions; no persistent entity relationship or client UX change here requires an ERD or mock. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Bind toolId when assigning ghApprovalClass to the one-argument Tool.approval callback. No companion rendering was supplied or visually verified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A stdin delivery failure proves that a secret was not set.","evidence":"§5 promises 'The secret is not set' for stdinError or nonzero exit. runShellBytes merely records a child.stdin error and the process exit; it supplies no remote transaction or rollback evidence. §2.2 itself correctly says that pipe delivery is not proof gh read the value. A remote mutation can succeed before a later local or network failure. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Report the mutation outcome as unknown when execution began and success cannot be established; require state verification before retrying. Test this distinction.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The flag-coverage test can account for every input field through a gh flag row.","evidence":"§2.7 and §3.3 fail any schema field without a flag row. Installed help shows gist rename uses positional '<id> <oldFilename> <newFilename>' and has only --help. Every family also adds synthetic op and cwd fields. The declared GH_FLAGS shape and rule provide no representation or exemption for these legitimate non-flag inputs, so the required test cannot pass honestly. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Model positional arguments and synthetic fields explicitly, separate them from flags, and check completeness across all three categories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream S005 acceptance criterion has a proposed proving test.","evidence":"DEF S005 defines ac1–ac6 for coverage, checked outputs, destructive approval, installation/sign-in failures, timeouts and legacy meaning. §6 maps each to corresponding coverage, schema/conversion, approval, failure, timeout and compatibility tests using the repository's node:test convention. These are proposed tests, not executed implementation evidence. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Retain the mapping while correcting the flag-inventory test and adding regression cases for the findings above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":4,"med":1,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T10:58:12.041Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
