10373	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-acd43b3eb73107bee0bee38490df2936","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:06:08.089Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The coverage scope and exclusions follow the upstream s5 decisions.","evidence":"DEF §6.5 requires named family tools without raw passthrough. docs/plans/tool-registry.md, 's5 decisions', explicitly accepts the listed exclusions and includes auth logout/switch and codespace cp/logs/ports. The proposed coverage and input inventories address that scope. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Retain these decisions as the coverage baseline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every accepted family input permits execution without prompting a person.","evidence":"Installed gh 2.46.0 help says `gh repo set-default` with no repository interactively selects a default, and `gh auth logout` with no selectors selects host/account via a prompt. The design accepts an empty set-default input and makes both logout selectors optional. Neither command offers --yes in its help. The design supplies no deterministic selection or rejection rule. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Require sufficient selectors or define deterministic resolution before execution; reject ambiguous selections. Test empty and multiple-account/repository cases.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current gh helper has a 30-second default, 4 MiB cap, and run view treats failed log retrieval as a successful answer.","evidence":"helpers.ts passes `timeoutMs: opts.timeoutMs ?? 30_000` and `maxBytes: opts.maxBytes ?? 4 * 1024 * 1024`. The complete ghRunViewTool body uses `logs.code === 0 ? logs.stdout : logs.stderr` and returns `success: true, data: { runId: id, jobs: payload.jobs ?? [] }`. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Keep the explicit compatibility exception for failed log retrieval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShellBytes can supply the subprocess outcome fields required by ghExec without changing shell-helper.ts.","evidence":"Read the complete runShellBytes implementation: it accepts stdin, independent stdout/stderr limits and AbortSignal, captures a stdout prefix, kills on stderr overflow, and returns spawnError, timedOut, stdoutTruncated, stderrOverflow, aborted, signal and stdinError. Its pre-aborted path returns without spawning. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Use these existing fields; distinguish pre-execution cancellation from cancellation after spawning when composing diagnostics.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The existing approval mask hides both secretValue and a field named key.","evidence":"approval-policy.ts masks keys matching `pass(word|wd)?|secret|token|api[-_]?key|account[-_]?key|access[-_]?key|private[-_]?key|credential|authorization|bearer|cookie`. `secretValue` matches; bare `key` does not. display() therefore includes the key text in arguments and the generic JSON preview. [files: src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Correct the reuse claim and explicitly design any required masking through field naming or a coordinated approval-contract change. Add approval-request assertions for both key-add tools.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"GhOpContracts defines exact output schemas for every new operation.","evidence":"The design specifies `gh_auth status => {op, hosts}`, `gh_config list => {op, entries}` and ruleset-list items without defining their nested shapes. callTool derives its result from `Static<T['outputSchema']>`, and executeTool validates result.data against that schema. These omissions leave the central typed contracts to implementation invention. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Specify the nested properties, types, optionality and keyValues projections for these outputs. Prose or tables suffice; no ERD is needed for these transient payloads.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The gist-edit contract covers noninteractive editing of existing file content.","evidence":"Installed `gh gist edit --help` exposes a filename positional and add/desc/filename/remove flags. The proposed edit input has selectors and metadata but no replacement content, content file or stdin delivery rule. Thus the named edit operation cannot express replacement of existing file contents without an editor. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Define the verified noninteractive content-edit path and its input/positionals, or document and obtain acceptance for excluding that capability. Test actual content delivery rather than argv alone.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The documented legacy diff/run result shapes and additive run truncation change agree with current code.","evidence":"Read ghPrDiffTool and ghRunViewTool completely. Diff returns `{ number: n, diffBytes: body.length, truncated }`; run view returns `{ runId: id, jobs: payload.jobs ?? [] }`. The design preserves these properties and explicitly adds run-view truncated. Neither function persists records, so these changes require no stored-record rewrite. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Preserve these shapes in fixture assertions, including the existing meaning of diffBytes as string length.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design consumes the existing executor, conversion and approval contracts rather than rebuilding adjacent stories.","evidence":"callTool accepts a TypedTool and delegates to executeTool. executeTool checks inputs before approval, validates successful data, then invokes hooks. convertText accepts schema/keyValues and serializes conversions with one escalation tier. The proposed gh-local wrappers and classifiers fit these extension points. docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly authorizes replacing the HLD's fixed 120-second limit with per-job limits. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Keep shared implementations outside this Story. File the acknowledged performance amendment to reconcile the HLD record.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The failure mapper classifies every termination by signal as rejected.","evidence":"runShellBytes returns `code: null` and signal for a signalled child. §2.3 lists rejected conditions as nonzero exit, stdin error, stderr overflow, abort, unmarked cut or failed probe, but does not explicitly include signal-only termination. §5 separately requires signal termination to be rejected with unknown outcome. These two normative descriptions disagree on a real helper outcome. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Add signal-only termination explicitly to the total classifier, with precedence for timedOut/aborted and an unknown-outcome suffix for mutations. Pin a fixture with signal set and all other failure flags false.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream s5 acceptance criterion has a planned proving test.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.5 ac1–ac6 with §6: coverage/input/argv tests address reachability; output and typed-call tests address checked results; approval tests address destruction; failure/session tests address installation/authentication; timeout tests address bounded execution; compatibility tests address existing ids and meanings. Existing approval-class-mapping.test.ts confirms the snapshot and per-input exception mechanisms the plan extends. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Retain the mapping and add focused tests for the contract defects identified above. These are planned tests, not verified implementation results. The analyzer request did not return a bundle before cancellation; conclusions here use direct code and documentation reads.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":5,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T11:06:08.089Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
433	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"7500d030354a40d4893dfb960571f012","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:08:23.224Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":6,"contentHash":"31d4ddc34dd686bd613c9d3c373461eb8b499b53a4c7372cfb3e3d8aeee62813"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":5,"med":0,"low":6}}}}}
11088	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-17c4a27663c2b8b3782577a5dc5d26bd","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:15:51.448Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed exclusions fully reflect the user's accepted reduction of ac1.","evidence":"DEF §6.5 ac1 requires every gh operation. docs/plans/tool-registry.md records the accepted exclusions, but does not accept gist content replacement or codespace cp --expand. The LLD nevertheless excludes both while explicitly acknowledging that acceptance is pending. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Resolve both exclusion decisions before treating ac1 coverage as complete; update the contracts and coverage inventory accordingly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every existing rename operation receives destructive approval.","evidence":"release.ts declares newTag and executes `if (str(input, 'newTag')) { argv.push('--tag', str(input, 'newTag')!); }`. The LLD lists gh_release_edit as common, while its input-dependent approval fields mention newName but omit newTag. Implementing that table leaves this rename able to run without destructive approval. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/release.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Classify gh_release_edit with newTag as destructive and add an approval test covering that existing input.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current gh helper defaults to 30 seconds and 4 MiB, and run-view treats failed log retrieval as successful output.","evidence":"helpers.ts passes `timeoutMs: opts.timeoutMs ?? 30_000` and `maxBytes: opts.maxBytes ?? 4 * 1024 * 1024` to runShell. The complete run-view execute body uses `const logBody = logs.code === 0 ? logs.stdout : logs.stderr` and subsequently returns success:true with data {runId, jobs}. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Retain these verified baselines in compatibility fixtures and explicitly record the proposed log-failure behaviour change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared byte runner, typed call helper and serial text conversion already provide the capabilities this story proposes to reuse.","evidence":"runShellBytes accepts stdin, independent capture limits and a signal, returning byte stdout plus stderrOverflow, aborted and stdinError. callTool derives input and result types from Static<T['inputSchema']> and Static<T['outputSchema']>. convertText accepts schema/keyValues, serializes conversions through takeSlot and supports escalation. The existing gh helper instead uses runShell. An analyzer request produced no bundle before being stopped; these conclusions use direct implementation reads. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Consume these existing interfaces without duplicating their execution, typing or conversion machinery.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed repository visibility command and project-wide JSON flag are accepted by installed gh 2.46.0.","evidence":"Read installed command help and exercised its parser with --help, without performing mutations. `gh repo edit --accept-visibility-change --help` exits 1 with 'unknown flag: --accept-visibility-change'. `gh project link --format json --help` exits 1 with 'unknown flag: --format'; unlink's complete help likewise has no format flag. The LLD requires that confirmation flag for visibility edits and says gh_project_manage sets --format json. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Specify version-correct arguments per operation. Omit unsupported flags and define output handling separately for project link/unlink.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The generic integer typing rule correctly represents numeric search filters.","evidence":"The LLD makes fields gh documents as numbers integers. Installed `gh search prs --help` documents comments, interactions and reactions as number filters, but explicitly demonstrates `--reactions=\">100\"`. Thus these are search expressions, not merely integers; the proposed rule rejects a supported unattended search. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Define search qualifier fields as expression strings where gh accepts comparisons or ranges; reserve integer schemas for actual counts and identifiers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Preserving all existing input schemas is compatible with the promised absence of passthrough fields.","evidence":"ghRepoCloneTool exposes `extraArgs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }`; execute forwards it verbatim using `argv.push('--', ...extra)`. approval-class-mapping.test.ts compares every original schema with the snapshot. The LLD simultaneously preserves those schemas/input meanings and requires a test that 'no registered gh tool takes a raw argv or passthrough field', without resolving this existing field. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/fixtures/approval-snapshot.json, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Choose and document an explicit compatibility decision for extraArgs, including any approved schema exception and named replacements. Align both compatibility and no-passthrough tests with that decision.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed family integration consumes shared contracts without requiring a redesign of their ownership or relationships.","evidence":"HLD §§4.2–4.5 assign typing/conversion/failure kinds to s2 and approval exchange to s3. The actual Tool, executor, callTool and approval-policy implementations expose the needed schema, approval-function and failure interfaces. LLD §4 describes the direction of consumption and leaves those implementations with their owners. These are execution dependencies rather than new persistent entity relationships; the prose/table adequately documents them. No companion visual is supplied or claimed as verified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Keep changes within the gh family and its tests; no additional relationship diagram is necessary for the integration described.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused runner exposes the failure signals needed for the proposed timeout, cancellation, stdin and overflow handling.","evidence":"Read the complete runShellBytes implementation: its timer marks timedOut and kills the process group; cancellation marks aborted; stdin's error listener records stdinError; stderr overflow marks stderrOverflow and kills; close preserves code and signal. These support the proposed explicit failure mapping and uncertainty messages. It also returns aborted immediately for a signal already aborted before spawning. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Preserve every runner field in the adapter and include the pre-aborted, never-spawned case in fixtures so messages do not imply execution necessarily began.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream s5 acceptance criterion has an identified proving test.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.5 ac1–ac6 with LLD §6: command coverage maps to coverage/input/family tests; declared results to schema/typed-call tests; destructive approval to approval tests; installation/sign-in failures to failure/live tests; deadlines to timeout tests; existing identities and meanings to compatibility tests. This verifies the proposed mapping, not execution of tests that have yet to be built. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Retain the six-criterion mapping while correcting the contract and test issues identified in this review.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed fake-gh and help-inventory tests independently prove command validity and absence of prompts.","evidence":"The fake binary uses canned behaviour and decides for itself when gh would prompt. Help inventory checks offered flags and schema fields, but does not validate all synthetic arguments against the real parser. Consequently the unsupported --format and --accept-visibility-change arguments confirmed in this review can survive those checks. The prompt-sweep mapping also says every codespace op except list/create requires codespace, contradicting the designed delete alternative `codespace | all`. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Add safe real-CLI parser checks for generated arguments and independently grounded prompt cases. Correct the delete-all test exception and ensure synthetic flags are validated against each command.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":3,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T11:15:51.448Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
