9880	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-2e28970a55e720db34e90f730706c7fb","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T12:36:09.076Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The exclusions, clone extraArgs exception and per-job timeout policy reflect upstream user decisions.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md records the accepted exclusions, explicitly includes auth logout/switch and codespace cp/logs/ports, retains clone extraArgs with destructive approval, and says the HLD performance line 'is to be read as this table'. These agree with the proposed scope. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"Retain these decisions and file the acknowledged performance amendment for traceability.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Legacy run view succeeds when its log subprocess fails, and clone forwards extraArgs after -- under common approval.","evidence":"actions.ts assigns 'const logBody = logs.code === 0 ? logs.stdout : logs.stderr' and subsequently returns success: true with {runId, jobs}. repo.ts declares approval: 'common', appends 'argv.push('--', ...extra)', and uses timeoutMs: 600_000. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts]","action":"Keep the explicit compatibility notes and regression fixtures for these behaviors.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"runShellBytes supplies the stdin, capture and cancellation information needed by the proposed gh adapter without changing shell-helper.ts.","evidence":"ShellBytesOptions accepts stdin and independent stdoutLimit/stderrLimit. ShellBytesResult exposes stdout bytes, stderrOverflow, aborted and stdinError. The implementation retains the stdout prefix with chunk.subarray(0, room), kills on stderr overflow and reports stdin write errors. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Reuse this helper and preserve its fields in GhOutcome.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing typed-call and conversion contracts support the proposed schema-preserving wrapper and serial conversion.","evidence":"callTool<T extends TypedTool> derives input and result from Static<T['inputSchema']> and Static<T['outputSchema']>. convertText accepts schema and keyValues, validates both shape and crossCheck, serializes through takeSlot(), and escalates from tools.convert to tools.convert.escalate. The analyzer returned an incomplete, low-confidence structural bundle; these conclusions come from reading the implementations. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts]","action":"Preserve concrete schema inference and use the existing conversion queue.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The release download input contract completely specifies valid requiredness.","evidence":"GhOpContracts makes tag, pattern and archive independently optional. Installed gh 2.46.0 help states: 'Without an explicit tag name argument ... --pattern or --archive is required.' The proposed contract therefore accepts an input with none of these fields that gh cannot execute successfully. The --help parser check cannot establish this execution-time constraint. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Require tag or a non-empty pattern list or archive, and add schema rejection and argv tests for the omitted-selector case.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The specified legacy diff/run payloads and additive run truncation field match current result shapes.","evidence":"ghPrDiffTool returns data: {number: n, diffBytes: body.length, truncated}; ghRunViewTool returns data: {runId: id, jobs: payload.jobs ?? []}. The design preserves these properties and explicitly identifies the additional run truncated field and changed failed-log behavior. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Retain payload compatibility tests and the documented behavioral exception.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The codespace permission notice can be placed in ApprovalRequest.reason through the existing sc4 tool extension points.","evidence":"buildApprovalRequest sets reason directly to either '${tool.id} can destroy work and always asks' or '${tool.id} needs approval'. buildApprovalGate supplies only preview title/content; ToolApprovalGate has no reason property. The design promises a codespace-specific approval request reason while leaving the s3-owned shared contract unchanged. [files: src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Specify the notice in buildApprovalGate preview content and adjust the test accordingly, or obtain an explicit shared-contract amendment for configurable reasons.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The family changes can be assessed through the supplied contract prose without requiring an ERD or UX mock.","evidence":"The HLD assigns gh family schemas, classifications and limits to s5 while executor approval, conversion and caller cutover remain separately owned. LLD sections 2–4 describe family-to-operation dispatch, per-operation ownership, shared helper dependencies, literal-op outputs and compatibility. No persisted entity relationship or client layout change is proposed, and no generated visual companion is claimed. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"No mandatory visual is needed for these relationships; resolve the specific approval contract mismatch above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed timeout, abort, signal, stdin-error and overflow paths have detectable inputs from the existing subprocess helper.","evidence":"runShellBytes separately records timedOut, aborted, signal, stdinError and stderrOverflow, including process-group termination. Its pre-aborted-signal branch returns aborted before spawning. The design conservatively warns of unknown mutation outcomes rather than claiming these flags prove a remote write did not occur. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Retain the explicit unknown-outcome handling; distinguish pre-spawn cancellation if more precise diagnostics are desired.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream s5 acceptance criterion has a proposed proving-test mapping.","evidence":"DEF s5 defines ac1–ac6 for coverage, checked outputs, destructive approval, installation/authentication failures, timeout messages and compatibility. LLD section 6 maps all six to named coverage/input/parser, schema/conversion, approval, failure, timeout and compatibility tests respectively. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Retain this mapping and incorporate the release-download constraint test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The failure precedence tests agree with the specified ghFailureOf algorithm.","evidence":"Section 2.3 permits the signal row only when there is no stdinError or stderrOverflow. The ac5 test instead requires 'signal beats stdinError beats stderrOverflow' using fixtures with two flags set. runShellBytes can report a signal together with stdinError or stderrOverflow, so these are meaningful combinations and the stated algorithm and tests require different results. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Choose one precedence and align the algorithm, error-path prose and paired-flag fixtures. Keep a separate signal-only termination fixture.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T12:36:09.076Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
